### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### Phase 2 — Auth, Users & Addresses Test Suite
### Sovva Backend (.NET 8)
###
### FLOW: These tests follow a user lifecycle:
###   Register → Profile → Add Address → Set Primary → Delete
###
### IMPORTANT: AuthMiddleware resolves Supabase JWT "sub" claim to
### sovva_user_id. User must exist in user_auth_mapping for most
### endpoints to work. Register creates this mapping.
###
### Token format: Supabase JWT with claims:
###   sub: <auth-uuid>        ← Supabase auth ID
###   aud: "authenticated"
###   role: "authenticated"
###   exp: <unix-timestamp>   ← expires in 1hr
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5257
@adminToken = eyJhbGciOiJFUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjE4OTNiMDM2LWYyMTAtNDM4Ni1hNWJkLTk5ODA3N2FhOWYwNyIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..WGeKXQVoqbHwBu5wJtUdQ4Ap2EnuKsmQlly4c7uxYgzqk1y1NTWpZva49lnHvr3KVG_QkU8qyX0xKQxRjFtc6A
@userToken = eyJhbGciOiJFUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6IjE4OTNiMDM2LWYyMTAtNDM4Ni1hNWJkLTk5ODA3N2FhOWYwNyIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..WGeKXQVoqbHwBu5wJtUdQ4Ap2EnuKsmQlly4c7uxYgzqk1y1NTWpZva49lnHvr3KVG_QkU8qyX0xKQxRjFtc6A

# These come from the JWT "sub" claim — must match the token
@userAuthId = 80079d73-3f15-4297-8d64-debff4764600
@mismatchAuthId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

# Set these after running the create/register requests
@userId = 1
@addressId = 1
@otherUserAddressId = 999


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 1. AUTHENTICATION
### Controller: AuthController
### Base route: /api/Auth
###
### Flow: Supabase OTP → get JWT → POST /register → user created
### AuthMiddleware adds sovva_user_id claim on subsequent requests
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### ─── 1.1 GET check-user-exists — happy path ─────────────────────
### AllowAnonymous + rate limited
### Expected: 200 OK → { exists: true/false }

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/check-user-exists?email=test@example.com HTTP/1.1

###

### ─── 1.2 GET check-user-exists — missing email ──────────────────
### Expected: 400 → { error: "Email is required" }

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/check-user-exists HTTP/1.1

###

### ─── 1.3 GET check-user-exists — empty email ───────────────────
### Expected: 400 → { error: "Email is required" }

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/check-user-exists?email= HTTP/1.1

###

### ─── 1.4 POST register — happy path ─────────────────────────────
### Requires valid Supabase JWT [Authorize]
### authId + email read from JWT sub+email claims — NOT sent in body
### Expected: 200 OK → { user: UserDto, isNewUser: true, message }
###
### Client sends ONLY: { name, phone? }

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/register HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Rishi Jain",
    "phone": "+918319910839"
}

###

### ─── 1.5 POST register — no auth ────────────────────────────────
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Test User"
}

###

### ─── 1.6 POST register — invalid token (no valid sub claim) ─────
### SECURITY: Server can't extract authId from JWT → 401
### NOTE: With a real invalid JWT the middleware returns 401 before reaching controller
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/register HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer invalid.jwt.token
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Attacker"
}

###

### ─── 1.7 POST register — duplicate (same authId already exists) ──
### Returns existing user — idempotent registration
### Expected: 200 OK → { user: UserDto, isNewUser: false, message: "User already registered" }

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/register HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Rishi Jain",
    "phone": "+918319910839"
}

###

### ─── 1.8 POST register — missing name (validation) ──────────────
### name is still required in body (only field client must send)
### Expected: 400 Bad Request → validation error

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/register HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "A"
}

###

### ─── 1.9 POST login — test endpoint ────────────────────────────
### AllowAnonymous — just returns info message
### Expected: 200 OK → { message: "Use Supabase authentication for login" }

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "test@example.com",
    "password": "anything"
}

###


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 2. USER PROFILE
### Controller: UsersController
### Base route: /api/Users
###
### NOTE: GetUserProfile uses ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier / "sub" claim
### to look up user by AuthId. GetDashboardSummary uses sovva_user_id.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### ─── 2.1 GET profile — happy path ───────────────────────────────
### Authenticated user — reads authId from JWT "sub" claim
### Expected: 200 OK → UserDto { userId, name, email, phone, role, walletBalance }

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/profile HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 2.2 GET profile — no auth ──────────────────────────────────
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/profile HTTP/1.1

###

### ─── 2.3 GET profile — expired token ────────────────────────────
### Use an expired JWT (1hr+ old) to test token validation
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized (JWT lifetime validation failed)
### Log: "JWT auth failed on /api/Users/profile: IDX10223: Lifetime validation failed"

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/profile HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIwMDAwMDAwMC0wMDAwLTAwMDAtMDAwMC0wMDAwMDAwMDAwMDAiLCJhdWQiOiJhdXRoZW50aWNhdGVkIiwicm9sZSI6ImF1dGhlbnRpY2F0ZWQiLCJleHAiOjE2MDAwMDAwMDB9.invalid

###

### ─── 2.4 GET dashboard-summary — happy path ─────────────────────
### Aggregated endpoint — 5 parallel queries
### Expected: 200 OK → DashboardSummaryDto
### Response cached for 60s (ResponseCache VaryByHeader=Authorization)

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/dashboard-summary HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 2.5 GET dashboard-summary — no auth ────────────────────────
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/dashboard-summary HTTP/1.1

###

### ─── 2.6 PUT profile — happy path ───────────────────────────────
### Update user name and phone
### Expected: 200 OK → updated UserDto
### DTO: UpdateUserProfileDto { name?, phone? }

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/profile HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Updated Name",
    "phone": "+919876543211"
}

###

### ─── 2.7 PUT profile — update name only ─────────────────────────
### Partial update — only name
### Expected: 200 OK → UserDto with updated name, unchanged phone

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/profile HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "New Name Only"
}

###

### ─── 2.8 PUT profile — no auth ──────────────────────────────────
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/profile HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Should Fail"
}

###

### ─── 2.9 PUT profile — empty name ───────────────────────────────
### Validation: Name cannot be whitespace-only
### Expected: 400 → { error: "Name cannot be empty" }

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/profile HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "   "
}

###

### ─── 2.10 PATCH user role — admin only ──────────────────────────
### Admin promotes/demotes users
### Expected: 200 OK → { message: "User 1 role updated to Admin" }

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{userId}}/role HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "role": "Admin"
}

###

### ─── 2.11 PATCH user role — invalid role ────────────────────────
### Expected: 400 → { error: "Invalid role. Must be one of: User, Admin" }

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{userId}}/role HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "role": "SuperAdmin"
}

###

### ─── 2.12 PATCH user role — self-demotion ───────────────────────
### Admin cannot remove their own Admin role
### Expected: 400 → { error: "You cannot remove your own admin role" }
### NOTE: Set userId to the admin's own ID for this test

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/{{userId}}/role HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "role": "User"
}

###

### ─── 2.13 PATCH user role — user token (not admin) ──────────────
### Expected: 403 Forbidden

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/Users/1/role HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "role": "Admin"
}

###


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 3. USER ADDRESSES
### Controller: UserAddressesController
### Base route: /api/UserAddresses
###
### FLOW (execute in order):
###   3.1  GET /primary → 404 (no addresses yet)
###   3.3  POST create address → 201 (save addressId)
###   3.5  GET /primary → 200 (first address auto-primary)
###   3.8  PUT /{id}/set-primary → 200
###   3.10 DELETE /{id} → when primary → 400
###   3.12 GET /{id} → other user's address → 403
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### ─── 3.1 GET primary — no addresses yet ─────────────────────────
### Expected: 404 → { error: "No primary address found. Please add an address." }
### Run this BEFORE creating any address

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/primary HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 3.2 GET all addresses — happy path ─────────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → array of UserAddressDetailDto (may be empty)

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 3.3 POST create address — happy path ───────────────────────
### Expected: 201 Created → UserAddressDetailDto + Location header
### SAVE the returned "id" as @addressId for subsequent tests
###
### DTO: CreateUserAddressDto {
###   serviceableLocationId (required),
###   wing?, block?, flatNumber (required),
###   floor?, additionalInstructions?, label?,
###   setAsPrimary (default false)
### }

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "serviceableLocationId": 1,
    "flatNumber": "A-401",
    "wing": "North",
    "block": "B",
    "floor": "4",
    "label": "Home",
    "additionalInstructions": "Ring doorbell twice",
    "setAsPrimary": true
}

###

### ─── 3.4 POST create address — no auth ──────────────────────────
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "serviceableLocationId": 1,
    "flatNumber": "B-202"
}

###

### ─── 3.5 POST create address — invalid serviceableLocationId ────
### Expected: 400 → { error: "..." } (InvalidOperationException from service)
### ServiceableLocationId 99999 doesn't exist

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "serviceableLocationId": 99999,
    "flatNumber": "C-303"
}

###

### ─── 3.6 POST create address — missing required fields ──────────
### Expected: 400 Bad Request (ModelState: flatNumber required)

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "serviceableLocationId": 1
}

###

### ─── 3.7 POST create second address — for set-primary test ──────
### Expected: 201 Created → save this id for set-primary test

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "serviceableLocationId": 1,
    "flatNumber": "D-505",
    "label": "Office",
    "setAsPrimary": false
}

###

### ─── 3.8 GET primary — after creating ───────────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → UserAddressDetailDto (the first address with setAsPrimary=true)

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/primary HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 3.9 GET address by ID — happy path ─────────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → UserAddressDetailDto

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/{{addressId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 3.10 GET address by ID — not found ─────────────────────────
### Expected: 404 → { error: "Address not found" }

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/99999 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 3.11 GET address by ID — different user's address ──────────
### Ownership check: address.UserId != current userId → Forbid
### Expected: 403 Forbidden
### Use an address ID that belongs to another user

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/{{otherUserAddressId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 3.12 PUT set-primary — happy path ──────────────────────────
### Switch primary to second address
### Expected: 200 OK → UserAddressDetailDto with isPrimary=true

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/{{addressId}}/set-primary HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 3.13 PUT set-primary — no auth ─────────────────────────────
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/{{addressId}}/set-primary HTTP/1.1

###

### ─── 3.14 PUT set-primary — address not found ───────────────────
### Expected: 404 → { error: "Address not found" }

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/99999/set-primary HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 3.15 PUT update address — happy path ───────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → updated UserAddressDetailDto

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/{{addressId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "serviceableLocationId": 1,
    "flatNumber": "A-401-Updated",
    "wing": "South",
    "label": "Home Updated"
}

###

### ─── 3.16 PUT update address — not found ────────────────────────
### Expected: 404 → { error: "..." } (KeyNotFoundException)

PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/99999 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "serviceableLocationId": 1,
    "flatNumber": "X-999"
}

###

### ─── 3.17 DELETE address — non-primary ──────────────────────────
### Expected: 200 OK → { message: "Address deleted successfully" }
### Delete the SECOND address (non-primary)

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/{{addressId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 3.18 DELETE address — primary address ──────────────────────
### Some services may block deleting the primary address
### Expected: 400 → { error: "..." } (InvalidOperationException)
###        or 200 OK if deletion is allowed

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/{{addressId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 3.19 DELETE address — no auth ──────────────────────────────
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/{{addressId}} HTTP/1.1

###

### ─── 3.20 DELETE address — not found ────────────────────────────
### Expected: 404 → { error: "Address not found" }

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/99999 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 3.21 GET validate address ──────────────────────────────────
### Checks if address change would affect active subscriptions
### Expected: 200 OK → ValidateAddressDto

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/{{addressId}}/validate HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

###

### ─── 3.22 GET validate address — no auth ────────────────────────
### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/UserAddresses/{{addressId}}/validate HTTP/1.1

###
